KG42.register("rules-10de495114df83091179a982",{"id":"38-bidirectional_ev_trading::v141-c-R006","paper":"38-bidirectional_ev_trading","record":{"rule_id":"v141-c-R006","mechanism_id":"M01","name":"Local energy product","process_stage":"bidding","market_meaning":"Surplus energy stored in a customer's EV battery is permitted to be sold to the aggregator. Scope: Customer-to-aggregator energy sales in the modeled power system. Condition: The customer has surplus energy stored in its EV's battery.","independence_rationale":"Relations governed by the approved function product.local_energy under the fixed relation-ownership template. Conditional branches retain their explicit scope in local constraints.","V":["product.local_energy"],"E":[],"omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"bidding","context_text":"Customer-to-aggregator energy sales in the modeled power system.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E03"]},"x":[{"variable_id":"v141-c-R006-x001","symbol":"x_{i,Tot}^{t}","meaning":"Total energy consumption of customer i at time-slot t, including residential-appliance and EV energy; a negative value denotes that the corresponding amount of energy is sold to the aggregator.","kind":"operational","domain":"Energy-consumption quantity per customer and time-slot (kWh); the source explicitly permits negative values to denote energy sold to the aggregator.","unit":"kWh","indices":["i ∈ I","t ∈ T"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E03","v141-b-g01-E02"]}],"theta":[],"phi":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R006-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Surplus energy stored in a customer's EV battery is permitted to be sold to the aggregator. Scope: Customer-to-aggregator energy sales in the modeled power system. Condition: The customer has surplus energy stored in its EV's battery.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["product.local_energy"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E03"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R006-C002","kind":"mathematical","role":"supporting","statement":"Source sign convention: a negative total energy value x_{i,Tot}^{t} means the corresponding amount of energy, -x_{i,Tot}^{t}, is sold to the aggregator. This is a direct equivalent formal statement of the supplied prose; the source gives no separate equation for the sale quantity.","expression":"x_{i,Tot}^{t} \u003c 0 \\;\\Rightarrow\\; -x_{i,Tot}^{t} \\text{ is sold to the aggregator}","formalization_origin":"equivalent_translation","template_id":null,"members":["product.local_energy"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R006-x001"],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E03"]}],"pi":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E03","location":{"location_id":"src-54c42059a7-p03-c1r4__v141-a-M01-participation","page":3,"printed_page":null,"section":"II. System Model","anchor_text":"overall energy scheduling of customer i by x = [xi]i∈I, where tri ¯xi = [xti,T ot, xti,App]t∈T . ch ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"We allow the bidirectional energy trading between customers and the aggregator, i.e., each customer can sell its energy to the aggregator when it has surplus energy stored in its EV's battery. Due to the energy trading capability, x_{i,Tot}^t may have a negative value, which means that the corresponding amount of energy is sold to the aggregator. For example, if x_{i,App}^t = 5 kWh and x_{i,Tot}^t = -10 kWh (accordingly x_{i,Tot}^t - x_{i,App}^t = -15 kWh), customer i discharges 15 kWh of energy from its battery to use 5 kWh for its own appliances and to sell 10 kWh to the aggregator at t-th time-slot."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E02","location":{"location_id":"src-54c42059a7-p03-c1r3__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":3,"printed_page":null,"section":"II. System Model","anchor_text":", pp tial appliances, xti,App. Compared to residential appliances that only consume energy, the EV h","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"focusing on the energy trading among customers, we consider a simplified appliance model where the amount of energy consumed by all the residential appliances of customer i during time-slot t is denoted by a single variable x_{i,App}^t. Then, we model customer i's utility function for its residential appliances during time-slot t as an increasing concave function U_i^t(x_{i,App}^t) of the amount of energy consumed by the residential appliances, x_{i,App}^t. Compared to residential appliances that only consume energy, the EV has the capability to charge and discharge energy into/from its built-in battery. The discharged energy can be used by other appliances, and thus x_{i,App}^t includes the energy consumed from the battery in the EV as well as the aggregator. We denote the total amount of customer i's energy consumption during time-slot t by x_{i,Tot}^t with the inclusion of the energy consumed by both the residential appliances and the EV. Accordingly, the difference between x_{i,Tot}^t and x_{i,App}^t, i.e., x_{i,Tot}^t - x_{i,App}^t, is the amount of energy charged/discharged into/from the EV's battery during time-slot t. Positive difference, x_{i,Tot}^t - x_{i,App}^t > 0, represents that the corresponding amount of energy is charged to the EV's battery during time-slot t, while negative difference, x_{i,Tot}^t - x_{i,App}^t \u003c 0, represents that the corresponding amount of energy is discharged from the EV's battery. We denote the overall energy scheduling of customer i by \\bar{x} = [\\bar{x}_i]_{i\\in I}, where \\bar{x}_i = [x_{i,Tot}^t, x_{i,App}^t]_{t\\in T}."}],"field_notes":{"empty_E_reason":"C explicitly supplied only source-backed unary facts for this function; other graph gaps remain reviewable.","empty_x_reason":null,"empty_theta_reason":"The source gives no fixed parameter, coefficient, or bound specific to this permission. The numerical example values (5 kWh, -10 kWh, -15 kWh) are illustrative, not parameters of the rule."},"evidence_basis":"explicit","implementation_status":"unimplemented","status":"needs_review","lead_ids":["v141-a-M01-participation","v141-a-M02-participation"],"extras":{"decision_anchor":"product.local_energy","graph_fact_supports":[[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E03","quote":"We allow the bidirectional energy trading between customers and the aggregator, i.e., each customer can sell its energy to the aggregator when it has surplus energy stored in its EV's battery."}]],"C2_formalization":{"graph_sha256":"447a7246a2ede6126771f014b50879c7e22f9d42e92e4927d2f60400ccdc754a","applicability":"formalized","reason":"The fixed rule is primarily a procedural permission for customer-to-aggregator energy sales. The supplied source also states a concrete sign convention for total energy x_{i,Tot}^{t}; that supported mathematical statement is formalized as a supporting constraint. No standalone bidding price, quantity, or optimization equation for the permission itself is supplied.","bindings":[{"object_id":"v141-c-R006-x001","node_ids":["product.local_energy"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"The declared total-energy variable is the source quantity whose negative sign represents customer-to-aggregator energy sale, so it binds to the frozen local-energy product node. No graph edge is asserted because C.1 supplied E=[] for this rule."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R006-C002","node_ids":["product.local_energy"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"The sign-convention constraint formalizes how the local energy product is represented in the source: negative total energy denotes energy sold to the aggregator. It uses only the existing product.local_energy node."}],"revision_requests":[]}},"quarantined_references":[]}});
